WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:04.000
Step two opens a matching window
until October thirty-first.

2
00:00:04.000 --> 00:00:08.217
Run the same fail fixture on October
thirtieth, inside the window,

3
00:00:08.217 --> 00:00:12.825
and the status is Warn: the blocks are
off, but an approved window says why.

4
00:00:12.825 --> 00:00:17.288
Run it on November first, the day
after the window closes, and it's Fail.

5
00:00:17.288 --> 00:00:19.013
Nobody edited anything.

6
00:00:19.013 --> 00:00:23.600
The window is a date, so a Warn
can never quietly become permanent.

7
00:00:23.600 --> 00:00:26.150
Step three feeds the check an export.

8
00:00:26.150 --> 00:00:29.180
The first two commands make
an inputs folder with an

9
00:00:29.180 --> 00:00:32.562
export that blocks soft match
but not hard-match takeover.

10
00:00:32.562 --> 00:00:37.137
The status is Fail with a count of
one: only the hard-match block is off.

11
00:00:37.137 --> 00:00:42.200
And the evidence's source is now Input,
with the export's file name as the query.

12
00:00:42.200 --> 00:00:44.064
That's the path the check prefers,

13
00:00:44.064 --> 00:00:47.930
because reading a file never needs
the Global Administrator role.
